	Channel ready threshold (in octets). The input half of the
	channel is ready when at least this much data is buffered.
	This field is only used when the
ref	cmd
	field holds
ref	kSMDCRxCtlNotifyOnData.
	If this value is negative, it represents the amount of space
	remaining. For example, the value <code>-256</code> means
	that the threshold is reached when there is space available
	for no more than 256 further octets.
	See also the document <a href="../an-data_transfer.html">Prosody
	application note: considerations for data transfer
	thresholds</a>.
