unstruct
	Performs a control operation on the input half of a data
	communications channel.
	<p>
	When the 
ref	cmd
	field holds
ref	kSMDCRxCtlNotifyOnData,
	the values 
ref	min_to_collect
	and
ref	min_idle
	configure the criteria used to determine when the input half
	of the channel is ready. There are two cases:
	<p>
	<table border>
	<tr>
		<th>min_idle</th>
		<th>Meaning</th>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><code>0</code></td>
		<td>The channel is ready when at least
ref	min_to_collect
		octets of data are waiting. It ceases to be ready
		when the amount waiting falls below
ref	min_to_collect.
		</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><code>T</code> != 0</td>
		<td>The channel is ready when any data can be 
		collected. Data becomes ready for collection when either
ref	min_to_collect
		octets of data are waiting, or data is waiting and no 
		further data has been received for a period of <code>T</code> mS.
	</tr>
	</table>
	<p>
	Note that, although times can be specified to the nearest
	millisecond, the measurement of time is limited to the epoch 
	period of the Prosody device.
